WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.201 --> 00:00:03.903
- Early on before the
league got shut down,

00:00:03.903 --> 00:00:06.306
the team had brought a doctor in

00:00:06.306 --> 00:00:07.407
to talk to everybody,

00:00:07.407 --> 00:00:08.241
tell everybody,

00:00:08.241 --> 00:00:09.075
okay, this is happening,

00:00:09.075 --> 00:00:10.343
a little bit about it.

00:00:10.343 --> 00:00:11.778
And one of the first
things he said was,

00:00:11.778 --> 00:00:13.747
masks do absolutely nothing.

00:00:13.747 --> 00:00:14.981
And he was like,

00:00:14.981 --> 00:00:16.950
I'm just letting you guys know

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:19.619
that apparently the way
he phrased it was like,

00:00:19.619 --> 00:00:21.254 align:start size:88% position:13%
I guess the COVID
particles were so small

00:00:21.254 --> 00:00:23.523
that they could pass through,

00:00:23.523 --> 00:00:24.457
pretty much most masks,

00:00:24.457 --> 00:00:26.092
especially cloth mask.

00:00:26.092 --> 00:00:27.260
- Yeah.

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:28.395
- So that was our first thing.

00:00:28.395 --> 00:00:29.662
So when he first said that,

00:00:29.662 --> 00:00:31.164
I was like, okay, I'm
not wearing a mask.

00:00:31.164 --> 00:00:32.665
And then you have these mask
mandates and things like that.

00:00:32.665 --> 00:00:34.200
I'm like, what is going on?

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:35.468
And so, yeah,

00:00:35.468 --> 00:00:36.302
it was pretty crazy.

00:00:36.302 --> 00:00:37.570
And in the bubble,

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:38.838 align:start size:81% position:19%
a lot of things
didn't make sense,

00:00:38.838 --> 00:00:39.806
but we kind of just
went along with it

00:00:39.806 --> 00:00:40.874
because we wanted to play.

00:00:40.874 --> 00:00:43.410
(bright music)

00:00:47.981 --> 00:00:49.482 line:0%
- I'm Dave Rubin

00:00:49.482 --> 00:00:51.184 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
and joining me today is a
professional basketball player

00:00:51.184 --> 00:00:54.487 line:0%
for the Orlando Magic and
author of the new book,

00:00:54.487 --> 00:00:57.123
"Why I Stand," Jonathan Isaac,

00:00:57.123 --> 00:00:59.092
welcome to the Ruben Report.

00:00:59.092 --> 00:01:00.060
- What's up, Dave.

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:01.094
Man, I'm excited to be here.

00:01:01.094 --> 00:01:01.928
Excited to talk to you.

00:01:01.928 --> 00:01:02.996
Let's go.

00:01:02.996 --> 00:01:04.464
- All right, let's do it.

00:01:04.464 --> 00:01:06.332
This is sort of your second
time on the Ruben Report

00:01:06.332 --> 00:01:09.869
because I was in
Orlando back in,

00:01:09.869 --> 00:01:10.703
what was it?

00:01:10.703 --> 00:01:11.938
That was end of October.

00:01:11.938 --> 00:01:13.306 align:start size:81% position:19%
And I was doing
this NatCon event.

00:01:13.306 --> 00:01:15.608 align:start size:97% position:3%
And I was like, hey,
Jonathan, Isaac's in Orlando.

00:01:15.608 --> 00:01:17.544
Maybe I can drag him on stage.

00:01:17.544 --> 00:01:21.748
And then you spoke in front
of about 500 conservatives.

00:01:21.748 --> 00:01:23.783
That was a little odd for you,

00:01:23.783 --> 00:01:26.119 align:start size:88% position:13%
but you pretty much
brought the house down.

00:01:26.119 --> 00:01:28.088
- But it was weird.

00:01:28.088 --> 00:01:29.956 align:start size:81% position:19%
You know, first
time kind of even,

00:01:29.956 --> 00:01:31.391
I mean, outside of like church,

00:01:31.391 --> 00:01:33.093 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
but like really speaking
in front of people

00:01:33.093 --> 00:01:34.194 line:0%
and then it being,

00:01:34.194 --> 00:01:37.030 line:0%
a conservative event.

00:01:37.030 --> 00:01:37.964
It was dope though.

00:01:37.964 --> 00:01:39.232
You know, everybody was great.

00:01:39.232 --> 00:01:40.467
I had a great time just
learning and listening.

00:01:40.467 --> 00:01:42.368 align:start size:84% position:16%
And you had the
chance to talk to you

00:01:42.368 --> 00:01:45.305
and kind of just continue
to push forward my message.

00:01:45.305 --> 00:01:48.675
- So let's start off with
some basketball stuff,

00:01:48.675 --> 00:01:51.911 align:start size:97% position:3%
'cause you know that my dream
was to be an NBA player.

00:01:51.911 --> 00:01:53.713
You accomplished my dream

00:01:53.713 --> 00:01:55.081
and you're pretty
good at what I do.

00:01:55.081 --> 00:01:56.683
That's what I said
to you on stage.

00:01:56.683 --> 00:01:59.886 align:start size:97% position:3%
You could be doing the
talking thing for a living.

00:01:59.886 --> 00:02:01.855
But you made it to the NBA

00:02:01.855 --> 00:02:03.723 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we also have
something else in common.

00:02:03.723 --> 00:02:05.959
We both have a torn ACL.

00:02:05.959 --> 00:02:09.529
So that has taken you out
for these last two seasons.

00:02:09.529 --> 00:02:11.531
Is left or right knee for you?

00:02:11.531 --> 00:02:12.365
- Left knee.

00:02:12.365 --> 00:02:14.501
- Left knee for me too.

00:02:14.501 --> 00:02:15.768
Tell me a little bit

00:02:15.768 --> 00:02:17.170
about just growing
up playing hoops.

00:02:17.170 --> 00:02:19.072 align:start size:84% position:16%
Did you always
wanna be in the NBA?

00:02:19.072 --> 00:02:20.974 align:start size:88% position:13%
Did you think you could
make it to the NBA?

00:02:20.974 --> 00:02:22.208
Just the challenges there

00:02:22.208 --> 00:02:24.811 align:start size:84% position:16%
before we get into
the book specifically.

00:02:24.811 --> 00:02:26.913
- Yeah. I mean the
book does a great job

00:02:26.913 --> 00:02:28.915
of just telling that
story of growing up

00:02:28.915 --> 00:02:30.350
in Bronx, New York,

00:02:30.350 --> 00:02:32.619 align:start size:97% position:3%
and playing at the rec center
in the park with my dad.

00:02:32.619 --> 00:02:34.320
And there is when
I really just kind

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:36.089 align:start size:84% position:16%
of like fell in
love with the game,

00:02:36.089 --> 00:02:38.391
not so much scoring
and all that stuff.

00:02:38.391 --> 00:02:40.527
Just the art of watching guys,

00:02:40.527 --> 00:02:41.528
do what they do on
the basketball court.

00:02:41.528 --> 00:02:42.962
I was like, man, it's so cool

00:02:42.962 --> 00:02:44.297
to watch them go left to right

00:02:44.297 --> 00:02:45.698
and all these different things.

00:02:45.698 --> 00:02:47.500 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I didn't know
anything about basketball

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:49.169
and the grand scheme of things.

00:02:49.169 --> 00:02:50.970
So nothing about college,
nothing about the NBA,

00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:52.572
nothing about conferences.

00:02:52.572 --> 00:02:54.107
There's one story in the book

00:02:54.107 --> 00:02:57.143 align:start size:97% position:3%
where I'm getting recruited
to go to college to play ball.

00:02:57.143 --> 00:02:58.378
And the coach is saying,

00:02:58.378 --> 00:02:59.679 align:start size:84% position:16%
do you know what
conference we're in?

00:02:59.679 --> 00:03:01.181
And I'm like, well,
what's a conference?

00:03:01.181 --> 00:03:02.815
(Dave chuckles)

00:03:02.815 --> 00:03:04.984
And I think that really speaks

00:03:04.984 --> 00:03:06.252
to how much I didn't even think

00:03:06.252 --> 00:03:07.987
that it could be a
possibility for me

00:03:07.987 --> 00:03:08.922
to get to the NBA.

00:03:08.922 --> 00:03:10.089
So it really, to me,

00:03:10.089 --> 00:03:11.491 align:start size:84% position:16%
is like a God thing
that I'm here,

00:03:11.491 --> 00:03:12.892
'cause I never believed in it.

00:03:12.892 --> 00:03:13.927
And so yeah,

00:03:13.927 --> 00:03:16.029
I mean I fell in love with it.

00:03:16.029 --> 00:03:17.497 align:start size:97% position:3%
I pretty much put everything
that I had into it,

00:03:17.497 --> 00:03:19.866 align:start size:97% position:3%
became the number one player
in the state of Florida,

00:03:19.866 --> 00:03:22.268
coming getting outta
high school to college

00:03:22.268 --> 00:03:24.304 align:start size:84% position:16%
and then was a six
pick to Orlando Magic.

00:03:25.471 --> 00:03:27.040
- Did you always
have great skills

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:30.176
or was it kind of learned
or a little bit of both?

00:03:30.176 --> 00:03:31.945
- I say all learned really.

00:03:31.945 --> 00:03:34.581 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, yeah, I love to
watch the guys on the TV,

00:03:34.581 --> 00:03:37.283 align:start size:97% position:3%
but I could never do anything
like that in the court.

00:03:37.283 --> 00:03:39.719
The first time I got
to play on an AAU team,

00:03:39.719 --> 00:03:41.821 align:start size:97% position:3%
they kicked me off of the
team without even telling me.

00:03:41.821 --> 00:03:43.690
And that's how bad I was.

00:03:43.690 --> 00:03:47.594 align:start size:97% position:3%
And so, my ride to practice
just stopped coming

00:03:47.594 --> 00:03:48.628
to pick me up.

00:03:48.628 --> 00:03:50.263
But it was definitely learned.

00:03:50.263 --> 00:03:51.998
Like I got my first coach

00:03:51.998 --> 00:03:53.633 align:start size:88% position:13%
that really was like
taking an interest in me

00:03:53.633 --> 00:03:56.436
because of my size, was Bora,

00:03:56.436 --> 00:03:57.704
and he's in the book as well.

00:03:57.704 --> 00:03:59.105
And you know, he
was the first one

00:03:59.105 --> 00:04:00.073 align:start size:94% position:6%
to teach me the
fundamentals and develop.

00:04:00.073 --> 00:04:01.007
And from there I kind of,

00:04:01.007 --> 00:04:02.075
it was just like riding a bike.

00:04:02.075 --> 00:04:03.009
I kind of just,

00:04:03.009 --> 00:04:04.510
because I was watching so much

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:08.481
and I found that passion in
liking the way that guys move

00:04:08.481 --> 00:04:09.515
that kind of just picked it up

00:04:09.515 --> 00:04:11.384
and kind of went from there.

00:04:11.384 --> 00:04:15.588 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Were you tall immediately
or late spurt or what?

00:04:15.588 --> 00:04:18.191
- I had a decent, like I guess,

00:04:18.191 --> 00:04:19.626
like a journey of a spurt.

00:04:19.626 --> 00:04:20.693
It wasn't all at one time.

00:04:20.693 --> 00:04:21.961
But I was always,

00:04:21.961 --> 00:04:24.264
more so the biggest
person in my class,

00:04:24.264 --> 00:04:25.832
especially through
the younger years.

00:04:25.832 --> 00:04:27.367
Once I got to high school,

00:04:27.367 --> 00:04:30.603 align:start size:88% position:13%
I was probably six foot,
6'1 my freshman year.

00:04:30.603 --> 00:04:31.971
And then each year,

00:04:31.971 --> 00:04:33.539
I jumped up three or four inches

00:04:33.539 --> 00:04:35.408
and then I got to seven foot.

00:04:36.743 --> 00:04:38.711 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Who are your heroes,
basketball heroes growing up?

00:04:38.711 --> 00:04:39.879
Who were the guys
that you were like,

00:04:39.879 --> 00:04:40.880
oh man, I wanna do that.

00:04:40.880 --> 00:04:43.416
I wanna model it after that.

00:04:43.416 --> 00:04:45.485
- You know, I loved KD.

00:04:45.485 --> 00:04:46.853
You know, great players still.

00:04:46.853 --> 00:04:47.787
But it's different now,

00:04:47.787 --> 00:04:48.955
being able to play against them.

00:04:48.955 --> 00:04:51.224
But yeah, I love the fact

00:04:51.224 --> 00:04:53.393
that he was such a big player,

00:04:53.393 --> 00:04:54.827
but was a guard pretty much.

00:04:54.827 --> 00:04:56.629
And so him, Dirk, PG,

00:04:56.629 --> 00:04:57.897
guys that I watch all the time.

00:04:57.897 --> 00:04:59.499
And I think I watched KD before

00:04:59.499 --> 00:05:02.135 align:start size:94% position:6%
every high school game,
before every college game.

00:05:02.135 --> 00:05:03.703
Yeah.

00:05:03.703 --> 00:05:04.904
- And tell me about that moment.

00:05:04.904 --> 00:05:06.939 align:start size:81% position:19%
You get the you're
at draft night

00:05:06.939 --> 00:05:09.008
and they say your name,

00:05:09.008 --> 00:05:10.343
and your life changes

00:05:10.343 --> 00:05:11.177
(Dave snaps)

00:05:11.177 --> 00:05:12.011
just like that.

00:05:12.011 --> 00:05:13.112
- Yeah, it was awesome.

00:05:13.112 --> 00:05:15.515
But for me, it was weird

00:05:15.515 --> 00:05:17.183
because everybody else around me

00:05:17.183 --> 00:05:19.419
seemed like they knew
what was going on.

00:05:19.419 --> 00:05:21.921 align:start size:88% position:13%
Like they were ready
for the moment they had,

00:05:21.921 --> 00:05:23.389 align:start size:84% position:16%
what they were
gonna do afterwards.

00:05:23.389 --> 00:05:24.791
They were gonna go party.

00:05:24.791 --> 00:05:26.125 align:start size:97% position:3%
They were gonna go celebrate
with their families.

00:05:26.125 --> 00:05:28.194
Like everyone took it in stride.

00:05:28.194 --> 00:05:29.429
But for me it was like,

00:05:30.463 --> 00:05:31.698
I don't know what to do.

00:05:31.698 --> 00:05:33.933
So I kind of, just
after I got drafted,

00:05:33.933 --> 00:05:36.536
I walked to a pizza
shop down the street.

00:05:36.536 --> 00:05:39.906
It was in New York
with coach Gates,

00:05:39.906 --> 00:05:41.341
who's a big part of my life.

00:05:41.341 --> 00:05:44.711
And one of my agents assistants

00:05:44.711 --> 00:05:46.479 align:start size:97% position:3%
and we got a pizza and I
went back to the hotel room,

00:05:46.479 --> 00:05:49.782
and sent my parent, my
family home on an Uber,

00:05:49.782 --> 00:05:51.818
and then went in my room.

00:05:51.818 --> 00:05:53.086
It was kind of just like a,

00:05:53.086 --> 00:05:53.920
it was weird.

00:05:53.920 --> 00:05:55.121
I didn't know,

00:05:55.121 --> 00:05:56.489
it just all went
by so fast as well.

00:05:57.657 --> 00:05:59.325
- And it must have been
pretty sweet for you.

00:05:59.325 --> 00:06:00.793
As you said,

00:06:00.793 --> 00:06:03.196 align:start size:97% position:3%
you played ball in Florida
then to be drafted by Orlando,

00:06:03.196 --> 00:06:04.697
you get to keep it in Florida,

00:06:04.697 --> 00:06:07.066
and you seem to have a great
connection with the state.

00:06:07.066 --> 00:06:08.134
- Yeah.

00:06:08.134 --> 00:06:09.502
I love the state of Florida

00:06:09.502 --> 00:06:11.170 align:start size:97% position:3%
and I've come to appreciate
it more and more,

00:06:11.170 --> 00:06:13.806
especially as the world has
gotten crazier and crazier.

00:06:13.806 --> 00:06:15.308
So, you know,

00:06:15.308 --> 00:06:16.743
I'm a fan of DeSantis and
what he is been able to do,

00:06:16.743 --> 00:06:19.278
but yeah, I love Florida.

00:06:19.278 --> 00:06:20.747
I'm, I'm glad that I'm here.

00:06:20.747 --> 00:06:22.382 align:start size:97% position:3%
I feel like it's a God Dame
thing for me to be here

00:06:22.382 --> 00:06:23.750
from middle school till now.

00:06:23.750 --> 00:06:25.485
And you know, I love the state.

00:06:25.485 --> 00:06:26.719
- All right.

00:06:26.719 --> 00:06:27.653
So let's, let's pick
it up right there.

00:06:27.653 --> 00:06:28.788
'Cause you mentioned DeSantis

00:06:28.788 --> 00:06:30.623
and then the Florida situation.

00:06:30.623 --> 00:06:34.694
And what put you
on my radar was,

00:06:34.694 --> 00:06:36.629
it's gotta be almost
two years ago now.

00:06:36.629 --> 00:06:38.598 align:start size:81% position:19%
Pretty early on
into the pandemic,

00:06:38.598 --> 00:06:40.400
NBA was one of the first leagues

00:06:40.400 --> 00:06:43.369 align:start size:88% position:13%
that just completely
shut down outta nowhere.

00:06:43.369 --> 00:06:44.604
In some ways,

00:06:44.604 --> 00:06:46.406
it was the first big
thing that did it,

00:06:46.406 --> 00:06:50.710 align:start size:97% position:3%
that then led to so many other
institutions closing down.

00:06:50.710 --> 00:06:53.513 align:start size:97% position:3%
You were one of the first
guys out there that was like,

00:06:53.513 --> 00:06:56.215 align:start size:88% position:13%
hey, could we slow
down with some of this?

00:06:56.215 --> 00:06:58.951
Or maybe I don't wanna
be necessarily injected

00:06:58.951 --> 00:07:00.186
with this thing

00:07:00.186 --> 00:07:02.422 align:start size:84% position:16%
or I'm gonna make some
choices for myself,

00:07:02.422 --> 00:07:03.689
et cetera, et cetera.

00:07:03.689 --> 00:07:05.024
So first, could you just
talk a little bit about

00:07:05.024 --> 00:07:07.126 align:start size:84% position:16%
what it was like
when you were hearing

00:07:07.126 --> 00:07:08.594
that things were gonna change

00:07:08.594 --> 00:07:10.196 align:start size:97% position:3%
and that the league was
shutting down before it got,

00:07:10.196 --> 00:07:11.798 align:start size:84% position:16%
'cause it all didn't
happen at once.

00:07:11.798 --> 00:07:13.699 align:start size:84% position:16%
That the vaccine stuff
started happening

00:07:13.699 --> 00:07:15.268
a little bit later than that.

00:07:15.268 --> 00:07:16.502
- Right.

00:07:16.502 --> 00:07:18.204
So I think what
happened at first

00:07:18.204 --> 00:07:20.139
was everybody was
just so afraid.

00:07:20.139 --> 00:07:21.607
Like right we were
getting those photos

00:07:21.607 --> 00:07:23.776 align:start size:94% position:6%
from China and some videos
and stuff like that.

00:07:23.776 --> 00:07:25.812
It was like, this thing
is coming to America.

00:07:25.812 --> 00:07:26.879
You know, when is
it gonna pop up?

00:07:26.879 --> 00:07:28.147
There was cases.

00:07:28.147 --> 00:07:30.716
And then you hear that a
player in the NBA has it

00:07:30.716 --> 00:07:32.819
and had spread it
to his teammates.

00:07:32.819 --> 00:07:34.220
And so, because of the way

00:07:34.220 --> 00:07:36.389 align:start size:84% position:16%
that it was portrayed
in the media.

00:07:36.389 --> 00:07:38.157
It was just such a fearful time.

00:07:38.157 --> 00:07:40.059
I feel like everybody was
walking on egg shells,

00:07:40.059 --> 00:07:42.228 align:start size:88% position:13%
thinking about when
they were gonna get it.

00:07:42.228 --> 00:07:44.397 align:start size:81% position:19%
And so once the
NBA had shut down,

00:07:44.397 --> 00:07:45.932
we had time to kind of just,

00:07:45.932 --> 00:07:48.100
now I think we went on
a quarantine really,

00:07:48.100 --> 00:07:49.635
I think right around that time,

00:07:49.635 --> 00:07:51.804
at least Florida
had like a curfew.

00:07:51.804 --> 00:07:53.606
It wasn't a complete lockdown,

00:07:53.606 --> 00:07:55.374 align:start size:97% position:3%
but we had a curfew that
you had to be in your house.

00:07:55.374 --> 00:07:56.943
And it was just a weird time.

00:07:56.943 --> 00:07:59.378
But you know, social
media wasn't a big help

00:07:59.378 --> 00:08:00.613
because of all the things

00:08:00.613 --> 00:08:01.547
that were spreading
and going around.

00:08:01.547 --> 00:08:03.149
And so, I just tried my best

00:08:03.149 --> 00:08:05.952
to try to take a step back
and just watch everything.

00:08:05.952 --> 00:08:09.021
There was an early
hesitation with me

00:08:09.021 --> 00:08:11.858 align:start size:97% position:3%
because of the way that
things were being portrayed.

00:08:11.858 --> 00:08:14.026 align:start size:88% position:13%
It seemed like
everything was so forced

00:08:14.026 --> 00:08:16.996 align:start size:84% position:16%
and made to be
fearful for everyone

00:08:16.996 --> 00:08:18.297
to kind of be running
around like chickens

00:08:18.297 --> 00:08:19.565
with their head cuts off.

00:08:19.565 --> 00:08:20.733
So I kind of just took
a step back and said,

00:08:20.733 --> 00:08:21.667
let me watch.

00:08:21.667 --> 00:08:22.702
And then we get to the bubble.

00:08:22.702 --> 00:08:23.536
And then after that,

00:08:23.536 --> 00:08:24.704
we get to, okay,

00:08:24.704 --> 00:08:25.938 align:start size:84% position:16%
now there's a
vaccine on the scene

00:08:25.938 --> 00:08:28.975
and that's that we
get a little later.

00:08:28.975 --> 00:08:30.042
- Right.

00:08:30.042 --> 00:08:31.277
So, all right.

00:08:31.277 --> 00:08:32.078 align:start size:84% position:16%
Let's talk about the
bubble situation.

00:08:32.078 --> 00:08:33.279
'Cause I think people

00:08:33.279 --> 00:08:34.080 align:start size:88% position:13%
or people that don't
pay attention to the NBA

00:08:34.080 --> 00:08:35.014
that are watching us,

00:08:35.014 --> 00:08:35.948
don't even know what that is.

00:08:35.948 --> 00:08:37.517
But they basically had you guys

00:08:37.517 --> 00:08:39.352
in your own sort of lockdown,

00:08:39.352 --> 00:08:42.788
so that the season could
kind of somewhat continue

00:08:42.788 --> 00:08:45.625 align:start size:88% position:13%
and sometimes you'd
have masks on the bench,

00:08:45.625 --> 00:08:47.126
but then you take
them off to play.

00:08:47.126 --> 00:08:48.961 align:start size:84% position:16%
So now you're
sweating on each other

00:08:48.961 --> 00:08:50.296
and spitting on each other

00:08:50.296 --> 00:08:51.731 align:start size:84% position:16%
and probably bleeding
on each other.

00:08:51.731 --> 00:08:53.165
But then when you sit down,

00:08:53.165 --> 00:08:54.433
you're wearing the mask.

00:08:54.433 --> 00:08:55.668
I mean, none of it
really made sense.

00:08:55.668 --> 00:08:57.703 align:start size:81% position:19%
Did coaches and
players talk about

00:08:57.703 --> 00:09:00.273
kind of the craziness
of the whole thing?

00:09:00.273 --> 00:09:01.407
- Yeah, we definitely did.

00:09:01.407 --> 00:09:03.743 align:start size:84% position:16%
And I think,
especially early on,

00:09:03.743 --> 00:09:05.811
like when we were first
getting into the bubble,

00:09:05.811 --> 00:09:09.115
everyone still, the
world is so afraid.

00:09:09.115 --> 00:09:11.183
So the NBA and all these
different organizations

00:09:11.183 --> 00:09:13.719
are trying to do all that
they can to kind of like,

00:09:13.719 --> 00:09:15.821
okay, we need to focus
on this and tackle this,

00:09:15.821 --> 00:09:17.323
but at the same time
we need guys to play.

00:09:17.323 --> 00:09:18.524
So what can we do?

00:09:18.524 --> 00:09:19.458
Okay.

00:09:19.458 --> 00:09:20.693
They wear the mask on the bench

00:09:20.693 --> 00:09:21.494
and they go into the
game and take it off.

00:09:21.494 --> 00:09:23.095
But it was such hysteria

00:09:23.095 --> 00:09:25.097 align:start size:84% position:16%
and just things
weren't making sense.

00:09:25.097 --> 00:09:26.566 align:start size:84% position:16%
And so, we definitely
had conversations

00:09:26.566 --> 00:09:29.468 align:start size:97% position:3%
about needing to test every
day and the mask thing.

00:09:29.468 --> 00:09:34.040
You know, early on before
the league got shut down,

00:09:34.040 --> 00:09:36.242
the team had brought a doctor in

00:09:36.242 --> 00:09:37.710 align:start size:84% position:16%
to talk to everybody,
tell everybody,

00:09:37.710 --> 00:09:38.878
okay, this is happening,

00:09:38.878 --> 00:09:40.146
a little bit about it.

00:09:40.146 --> 00:09:41.714
And one of the first
things he said was,

00:09:41.714 --> 00:09:43.449
masks do absolutely nothing.

00:09:43.449 --> 00:09:44.283
(Dave chuckles)

00:09:44.283 --> 00:09:45.751
And he was like,

00:09:45.751 --> 00:09:48.387 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm just letting you guys
know that apparently,

00:09:48.387 --> 00:09:49.555
the way he phrased it was like,

00:09:49.555 --> 00:09:51.691 align:start size:88% position:13%
I guess the COVID
particles were so small

00:09:51.691 --> 00:09:54.393 align:start size:97% position:3%
that they could pass through
pretty much most masks,

00:09:54.393 --> 00:09:56.028
especially cloth mask.

00:09:56.028 --> 00:09:57.196
- Yeah.

00:09:57.196 --> 00:09:58.364
- So that was our first thing.

00:09:58.364 --> 00:09:59.632
So when he first said that,

00:09:59.632 --> 00:10:00.466
I was like, okay,

00:10:00.466 --> 00:10:01.701
I'm not wearing a mask.

00:10:01.701 --> 00:10:02.501
And then you have
these mask mandates

00:10:02.501 --> 00:10:03.436
and things like that.

00:10:03.436 --> 00:10:04.103
I'm like, what is going on?

00:10:04.103 --> 00:10:05.371
And so, yeah.

00:10:05.371 --> 00:10:07.173 align:start size:84% position:16%
It was pretty crazy
in the bubble.

00:10:07.173 --> 00:10:08.407 align:start size:81% position:19%
A lot of things
didn't make sense,

00:10:08.407 --> 00:10:09.342
but we kind of just
went along with it

00:10:09.342 --> 00:10:10.676
because we wanted to play.

00:10:10.676 --> 00:10:11.944
- Were you surprised the way

00:10:11.944 --> 00:10:14.046 line:0%
some guys just kind
of took the orders,

00:10:14.046 --> 00:10:15.581 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
even though they
thought it didn't work,

00:10:15.581 --> 00:10:17.683 line:0%
or the fact that
you guys are mostly

00:10:17.683 --> 00:10:18.818 line:0%
in your mid twenties

00:10:18.818 --> 00:10:20.686
at the peak of physical health,

00:10:20.686 --> 00:10:22.755 align:start size:88% position:13%
like your
cardiovascular is better

00:10:22.755 --> 00:10:24.857 align:start size:84% position:16%
than basically
anyone on the planet.

00:10:24.857 --> 00:10:27.193
You all eat right,
et cetera, et cetera,

00:10:27.193 --> 00:10:29.662 align:start size:97% position:3%
yet everybody started
doing all this crazy stuff.

00:10:30.596 --> 00:10:32.331
- I wouldn't say
I was surprised.

00:10:32.331 --> 00:10:35.167
I mean, societal
pressure is tough.

00:10:35.167 --> 00:10:37.103
I mean, it works.

00:10:37.103 --> 00:10:39.739 align:start size:97% position:3%
And especially when you have
people that are higher up

00:10:39.739 --> 00:10:42.108 align:start size:84% position:16%
or just people
around you who are,

00:10:42.108 --> 00:10:45.578 align:start size:97% position:3%
who kind of adopt this
mainstream idea or ideology

00:10:45.578 --> 00:10:46.979
and kind of just run with it.

00:10:46.979 --> 00:10:48.547
So I don't think
I was surprised.

00:10:48.547 --> 00:10:49.849
Even myself early on,

00:10:49.849 --> 00:10:52.018
I was like, okay, this
is what we have to do.

00:10:52.018 --> 00:10:53.786 align:start size:84% position:16%
It wasn't until
things got later on

00:10:53.786 --> 00:10:55.087
and we get out the bubble,

00:10:55.087 --> 00:10:56.922
and then the vaccine
starts coming around.

00:10:56.922 --> 00:10:59.158
And then I can just see the,

00:10:59.158 --> 00:11:00.726
just how much it
was being pushed.

00:11:00.726 --> 00:11:03.462
And you have all the
people on social media,

00:11:03.462 --> 00:11:05.264 align:start size:84% position:16%
the demeaning everyone
and all this stuff.

00:11:05.264 --> 00:11:07.667
And then, the thing about
the Rolling Stone article

00:11:07.667 --> 00:11:08.601
happens to me.

00:11:08.601 --> 00:11:10.136
And that's when I'm like,

00:11:10.136 --> 00:11:11.671
okay, this thing is really
not just about a vaccine.

00:11:11.671 --> 00:11:13.439 align:start size:81% position:19%
It's political,
there's an agenda.

00:11:13.439 --> 00:11:14.840
There's a bias to it.

00:11:14.840 --> 00:11:15.775
But I, no,

00:11:15.775 --> 00:11:16.809
I wouldn't surprise everybody

00:11:16.809 --> 00:11:18.210
kind of went along with it.

00:11:18.210 --> 00:11:19.478
- All right.

00:11:19.478 --> 00:11:20.946
So let's get to that
part in just a sec,

00:11:20.946 --> 00:11:22.148 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I just wanna do a
little more on the bubble.

00:11:22.148 --> 00:11:23.082 align:start size:84% position:16%
So again, for people
that don't know,

00:11:23.082 --> 00:11:25.117
so they basically had you guys,

00:11:25.117 --> 00:11:27.720
were you all pretty
much in one hotel

00:11:27.720 --> 00:11:29.622
and had to limit who
was coming in and out?

00:11:29.622 --> 00:11:30.856
Like they really,

00:11:30.856 --> 00:11:32.425
the idea was that you
weren't gonna basically

00:11:32.425 --> 00:11:35.761 align:start size:88% position:13%
see anybody else,
wives, kids, et cetera,

00:11:35.761 --> 00:11:37.229 align:start size:88% position:13%
and that you would play
against each other,

00:11:37.229 --> 00:11:38.497
and that's it.

00:11:38.497 --> 00:11:39.699
But I've heard from
some other players,

00:11:39.699 --> 00:11:42.068
that's not exactly
how the thing worked.

00:11:42.068 --> 00:11:43.869
- Well, it was three hotels.

00:11:43.869 --> 00:11:46.706
And so you had teams split
up in these three hotels

00:11:46.706 --> 00:11:48.407 align:start size:84% position:16%
and pretty much
the order was like,

00:11:48.407 --> 00:11:49.442
you're not allowed to leave.

00:11:49.442 --> 00:11:51.577
Once you come in, that's it.

00:11:51.577 --> 00:11:53.145
As the bubble kind of went on

00:11:53.145 --> 00:11:54.680
and we got to the playoffs,

00:11:54.680 --> 00:11:56.415 align:start size:97% position:3%
I think they allowed some
people's families to come in

00:11:56.415 --> 00:11:57.850
or just their wives or
something like that.

00:11:57.850 --> 00:12:00.186
But early on, it
was like strict.

00:12:00.186 --> 00:12:01.353
We test every day.

00:12:01.353 --> 00:12:03.189 align:start size:88% position:13%
I think we were testing
like twice a day.

00:12:03.189 --> 00:12:04.356
I'm not even really sure,

00:12:04.356 --> 00:12:06.125
but you're testing every day.

00:12:07.293 --> 00:12:08.327
You know, they had
a lounge set up,

00:12:08.327 --> 00:12:09.562
they had a barbershop for.

00:12:09.562 --> 00:12:12.465
So they tried to kind of
help it be worthwhile,

00:12:12.465 --> 00:12:14.266
but it was just tough to kind

00:12:14.266 --> 00:12:16.001 align:start size:88% position:13%
of just be in the hotel
room all the time.

00:12:16.001 --> 00:12:17.403
But yeah, nothing in,

00:12:17.403 --> 00:12:19.038
nothing out of food all there.

00:12:19.038 --> 00:12:22.041
So it was really
like a jail lowkey.

00:12:22.041 --> 00:12:23.776
- I mean, I heard some rumors

00:12:23.776 --> 00:12:25.344
that people were
coming and going,

00:12:25.344 --> 00:12:29.315
and able to get some lady
friends inside et cetera.

00:12:29.315 --> 00:12:30.816
- And some people
got in trouble.

00:12:30.816 --> 00:12:32.384 align:start size:84% position:16%
You know, some people
who got caught,

00:12:32.384 --> 00:12:34.186
I didn't hear anything

00:12:34.186 --> 00:12:36.122 align:start size:94% position:6%
about guys actually being
successful with that,

00:12:36.122 --> 00:12:37.323
but I did hear the story

00:12:37.323 --> 00:12:40.126
about one guy trying
and getting in trouble.

00:12:40.126 --> 00:12:40.926
- Right.

00:12:40.926 --> 00:12:41.994
- So, okay.

00:12:41.994 --> 00:12:43.362
So then the bubble passes

00:12:43.362 --> 00:12:45.965 align:start size:97% position:3%
and now things start
shifting towards the vaccine.

00:12:45.965 --> 00:12:48.701
And that's where
that video of you.

00:12:48.701 --> 00:12:49.935
What month?

00:12:49.935 --> 00:12:51.737 align:start size:84% position:16%
Do you remember
what month that was?

00:12:51.737 --> 00:12:52.705
- No, not at all.

00:12:52.705 --> 00:12:53.939
- All right.

00:12:53.939 --> 00:12:55.441 align:start size:84% position:16%
So it's about a
year and a half ago.

00:12:55.441 --> 00:12:56.709 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, it was at the
height of the whole thing.

00:12:56.709 --> 00:12:59.879
And basically, you
gave a spectacular,

00:12:59.879 --> 00:13:00.813
you know what?

00:13:00.813 --> 00:13:02.014
We'll lay it in right here.

00:13:02.014 --> 00:13:04.517 align:start size:84% position:16%
We're gonna lay in
the speech right here,

00:13:04.517 --> 00:13:05.985
so people can listen to it.

00:13:05.985 --> 00:13:09.922 align:start size:97% position:3%
- It is my belief that the
vaccine status of every person

00:13:09.922 --> 00:13:13.526
should be their own choice
and completely up to them

00:13:13.526 --> 00:13:16.328 align:start size:88% position:13%
without bullying,
without being pressured

00:13:16.328 --> 00:13:18.364 align:start size:84% position:16%
or without being
forced into doing so.

00:13:18.364 --> 00:13:21.200
I'm not ashamed to say
that I'm uncomfortable

00:13:21.200 --> 00:13:23.736 align:start size:84% position:16%
with taking the
vaccine at this time.

00:13:23.736 --> 00:13:25.204 align:start size:81% position:19%
I think that we're
all different.

00:13:25.204 --> 00:13:26.438
We all come from
different places.

00:13:26.438 --> 00:13:28.040 align:start size:84% position:16%
We've all had
different experiences

00:13:28.040 --> 00:13:29.909
and hold dear to
different beliefs.

00:13:29.909 --> 00:13:32.077 align:start size:84% position:16%
And what it is that
you do with your body,

00:13:32.077 --> 00:13:34.346 align:start size:88% position:13%
when it comes to putting
medicine in there,

00:13:34.346 --> 00:13:36.248
should be your choice,

00:13:36.248 --> 00:13:38.818
free of the ridicule and
the opinion of others.

00:13:38.818 --> 00:13:41.487
I've had COVID in the past.

00:13:41.487 --> 00:13:44.356 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so, our understanding
of antibodies,

00:13:44.356 --> 00:13:45.591
of natural immunity,

00:13:45.591 --> 00:13:48.460
has changed a great deal

00:13:48.460 --> 00:13:49.695
from the onset of the pandemic,

00:13:49.695 --> 00:13:50.996
and it's still evolving.

00:13:52.231 --> 00:13:55.434
I understand that the
vaccine would help

00:13:55.434 --> 00:13:56.836
if you catch COVID

00:13:56.836 --> 00:13:59.271
and you'll be able
to have less symptoms

00:13:59.271 --> 00:14:00.539
from contracting it.

00:14:00.539 --> 00:14:02.041
But with me having
COVID in the past,

00:14:02.041 --> 00:14:05.811
and to having antibodies
with my current age group

00:14:05.811 --> 00:14:08.981
and physical fitness level,

00:14:08.981 --> 00:14:11.584 align:start size:84% position:16%
it's not necessarily
a fear of mine,

00:14:11.584 --> 00:14:12.885
taking the vaccine.

00:14:14.119 --> 00:14:15.654
Like I said,

00:14:15.654 --> 00:14:18.424
it would decrease my chances
of having a severe reaction,

00:14:18.424 --> 00:14:21.760
but it does open me up to
the albeit rare chance,

00:14:21.760 --> 00:14:23.963 align:start size:94% position:6%
but the possibility of
having an adverse reaction

00:14:23.963 --> 00:14:25.331
to the vaccine itself.

00:14:26.765 --> 00:14:30.803
I don't believe that being
unvaccinated means infected

00:14:30.803 --> 00:14:33.939
or being vaccinated
means uninfected.

00:14:33.939 --> 00:14:36.075
You can still catch COVID

00:14:36.075 --> 00:14:37.877
with or with not
having the vaccine.

00:14:39.111 --> 00:14:40.179
I would say honestly,

00:14:40.179 --> 00:14:42.414
the craziness of it all

00:14:42.414 --> 00:14:44.617
in terms of not
being able to say

00:14:44.617 --> 00:14:46.285 align:start size:88% position:13%
that it should be
everybody's fair choice

00:14:46.285 --> 00:14:49.922 align:start size:84% position:16%
without being demeaned
or talked crazy to,

00:14:49.922 --> 00:14:54.426
doesn't make one comfortable
to do what that person is,

00:14:54.426 --> 00:14:56.095
telling them to do.

00:14:57.863 --> 00:14:59.131
Yeah.

00:14:59.131 --> 00:15:00.366
I would say, that's a
couple of the reasons

00:15:00.366 --> 00:15:02.935
that I would say I'm
hesitant at this time.

00:15:02.935 --> 00:15:04.370
But at the end of the day,

00:15:04.370 --> 00:15:05.804
I don't feel that it is.

00:15:05.804 --> 00:15:08.274 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, anyone's reason
to come out and say,

00:15:08.274 --> 00:15:09.742
well, this is why,

00:15:09.742 --> 00:15:11.477 align:start size:97% position:3%
or this is not why it should
just be their decision.

00:15:11.477 --> 00:15:13.646 align:start size:84% position:16%
And you know, loving
your neighbors,

00:15:13.646 --> 00:15:15.147
not just loving those
that agree with you,

00:15:15.147 --> 00:15:18.684
or look like you are moving
the same way that you do.

00:15:18.684 --> 00:15:20.552
It's loving those who don't.

00:15:20.552 --> 00:15:21.954
- So that right there.

00:15:21.954 --> 00:15:24.189
I mean, you laid out
more common sense,

00:15:24.189 --> 00:15:26.892
decency, and thoughtful analysis

00:15:26.892 --> 00:15:30.562 align:start size:84% position:16%
than pretty much
anything I saw on CNN.

00:15:30.562 --> 00:15:31.497
And that's where I was like,

00:15:31.497 --> 00:15:32.898
man, I gotta talk to this guy.

00:15:34.033 --> 00:15:36.535
- Yeah. I mean, so
again, like early on,

00:15:36.535 --> 00:15:37.970
like me just trying
to take a step back

00:15:37.970 --> 00:15:40.105 align:start size:88% position:13%
and just see everything
that was going on.

00:15:40.105 --> 00:15:41.573
I was like, okay,

00:15:41.573 --> 00:15:44.610
they're saying that the virus
has a 99.97 survival rate.

00:15:44.610 --> 00:15:45.844
I'm young, you know,

00:15:45.844 --> 00:15:47.980
people who are older
and have comorbidities

00:15:47.980 --> 00:15:50.282 align:start size:97% position:3%
or obese are really
struggling with this thing.

00:15:50.282 --> 00:15:51.650
So I just said, you know,

00:15:51.650 --> 00:15:54.553 align:start size:88% position:13%
as I saw how much the
vaccine was being pushed

00:15:54.553 --> 00:15:55.721
and forced on everybody,

00:15:55.721 --> 00:15:58.190 align:start size:88% position:13%
and then you see social
media and people,

00:15:58.190 --> 00:16:00.092
calling people crazy for
not wanting to take it,

00:16:00.092 --> 00:16:02.261 align:start size:97% position:3%
or even just being hesitant
or asking questions.

00:16:02.261 --> 00:16:03.729
And then you have
people's medical

00:16:03.729 --> 00:16:05.397 align:start size:88% position:13%
and religious
exemptions being denied,

00:16:05.397 --> 00:16:06.365
and people losing their jobs.

00:16:06.365 --> 00:16:07.466
I was like, man, this is insane.

00:16:07.466 --> 00:16:08.634
This isn't right.

00:16:08.634 --> 00:16:09.501 align:start size:84% position:16%
And so I just said,
you know what,

00:16:09.501 --> 00:16:10.903
I'm young, I'm healthy.

00:16:10.903 --> 00:16:12.972 align:start size:97% position:3%
I don't have any side effects
or anything like that.

00:16:12.972 --> 00:16:14.139
I don't see the wisdom

00:16:14.139 --> 00:16:15.374 align:start size:84% position:16%
in putting something
into my body.

00:16:15.374 --> 00:16:17.609
That's not gonna stop me
from getting the virus

00:16:17.609 --> 00:16:19.545
or transmitting it
to someone else.

00:16:19.545 --> 00:16:21.113
That's just where I'm at
and I'm not gonna do it.

00:16:21.113 --> 00:16:22.214
And you know, at the same time,

00:16:22.214 --> 00:16:23.749
I want it to be a hope

00:16:23.749 --> 00:16:25.951
and a voice for other people
who are going through this,

00:16:25.951 --> 00:16:27.453
who didn't have a platform.

00:16:27.453 --> 00:16:29.722
- Was that just a normal
postgame press conference?

00:16:29.722 --> 00:16:31.357 align:start size:84% position:16%
Or were you planning
on doing that?

00:16:31.357 --> 00:16:32.391
Or how did that even happen?

00:16:32.391 --> 00:16:33.325
Were you thinking about,

00:16:33.325 --> 00:16:34.760
hey, I gotta say something.

00:16:34.760 --> 00:16:36.228
- No, it was actually perfect

00:16:36.228 --> 00:16:38.364 align:start size:84% position:16%
because the Rolling
Stone article.

00:16:38.364 --> 00:16:41.200
So, if around that time,

00:16:41.200 --> 00:16:42.601
the team calls me and they say,

00:16:42.601 --> 00:16:44.136 align:start size:94% position:6%
hey, you know, the
Rolling Stone wants to do

00:16:44.136 --> 00:16:46.505
an interview with you about
everything that's going on.

00:16:46.505 --> 00:16:47.740
I'm saying, cool.

00:16:47.740 --> 00:16:49.641
So I get on the phone
with him and he's like,

00:16:49.641 --> 00:16:50.576
you're unvaccinated.

00:16:50.576 --> 00:16:51.810
And I'm thinking to myself like,

00:16:51.810 --> 00:16:52.845
how do you even know
that I'm unvaccinated?

00:16:52.845 --> 00:16:54.213
Whatever.

00:16:54.213 --> 00:16:56.048 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Welcome to the mainstream
media, my friend.

00:16:56.048 --> 00:16:57.516
- Right.

00:16:57.516 --> 00:16:59.118 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, yeah, it was actually
a great conversation.

00:16:59.118 --> 00:17:00.519 align:start size:81% position:19%
Like we're talking
and he's like,

00:17:00.519 --> 00:17:01.520
oh, you know what?

00:17:01.520 --> 00:17:02.821
I agree with you
on that and all,

00:17:02.821 --> 00:17:04.056
that's a good point.

00:17:04.056 --> 00:17:05.290
And I pretty much
laid out to him

00:17:05.290 --> 00:17:07.493
exactly what I went on
to say the next day.

00:17:07.493 --> 00:17:09.928 align:start size:88% position:13%
And so, but the article
drops that night,

00:17:09.928 --> 00:17:10.863
like the Sunday night.

00:17:10.863 --> 00:17:12.331
And it says,

00:17:12.331 --> 00:17:15.501
Jonathan Isaac came to his
vaccination status, whatever,

00:17:15.501 --> 00:17:17.936 align:start size:88% position:13%
by watching Donald
Trump press conferences

00:17:17.936 --> 00:17:19.538
and studying black history.

00:17:19.538 --> 00:17:21.573
And that's when I'm
like, oh my gosh.

00:17:21.573 --> 00:17:23.042
- Yep.

00:17:23.042 --> 00:17:24.276 align:start size:97% position:3%
- And everybody's on social
media calling me crazy.

00:17:24.276 --> 00:17:27.212 align:start size:81% position:19%
And I sound stupid
in the article.

00:17:27.212 --> 00:17:29.348
But the next day was media day.

00:17:29.348 --> 00:17:30.582
So Monday is media day.

00:17:30.582 --> 00:17:32.451 align:start size:84% position:16%
And I was expecting
the question.

00:17:32.451 --> 00:17:34.520
I was on the phone with
my pastor that night.

00:17:34.520 --> 00:17:35.754
And he was like,

00:17:35.754 --> 00:17:36.688
well, you have an
opportunity to talk

00:17:36.688 --> 00:17:37.623
about it tomorrow at media day,

00:17:37.623 --> 00:17:38.824
have to ask you about it.

00:17:38.824 --> 00:17:40.125 align:start size:88% position:13%
And I just kind of tried
to lay it out there.

00:17:40.125 --> 00:17:41.326
- Yeah.

00:17:41.326 --> 00:17:42.261 align:start size:84% position:16%
So that was your
first time being hit

00:17:42.261 --> 00:17:43.796
by the media like that, huh?

00:17:43.796 --> 00:17:44.997
Welcome to the party.

00:17:45.831 --> 00:17:47.266
- Well, it was my first,

00:17:47.266 --> 00:17:48.734
not being hit by the media

00:17:48.734 --> 00:17:49.635
because then you have the whole
standing in the bubble thing

00:17:49.635 --> 00:17:50.636
that was before that.

00:17:50.636 --> 00:17:52.304
That was in June of 2020.

00:17:52.304 --> 00:17:53.839
But it was the first time like-

00:17:53.839 --> 00:17:54.773
- Oh, right.

00:17:54.773 --> 00:17:56.041
So yeah, wait, let's back up.

00:17:56.041 --> 00:17:57.342
Tell people about
that first, right.

00:17:57.342 --> 00:17:58.877
We skipped over something big.

00:17:59.745 --> 00:18:01.246
- Well, yeah.

00:18:01.246 --> 00:18:04.383 align:start size:97% position:3%
Well, so around the time of
what happened to George Floyd,

00:18:04.383 --> 00:18:06.318
as tragic and as
wrong as it was,

00:18:06.318 --> 00:18:08.487 align:start size:88% position:13%
there was a lot of
pressure on NBA players

00:18:08.487 --> 00:18:09.988
going into the bubble,

00:18:09.988 --> 00:18:12.024
to have to kneel for
the national anthem

00:18:12.024 --> 00:18:13.725
and the wear the Black
Lives Matter T-shirt.

00:18:13.725 --> 00:18:15.661 align:start size:88% position:13%
But again, I same
thing with the vaccine,

00:18:15.661 --> 00:18:16.595
I tried to step back and say,

00:18:16.595 --> 00:18:18.397
okay, what is the right way

00:18:18.397 --> 00:18:19.932
for me to respond in this moment

00:18:19.932 --> 00:18:21.633
that I feel would
bring real change?

00:18:21.633 --> 00:18:23.268 align:start size:84% position:16%
And for some people
in that moment,

00:18:23.268 --> 00:18:24.470
it was kneeling and
wearing the t-shirt.

00:18:24.470 --> 00:18:25.471
But for me, it wasn't.

00:18:25.471 --> 00:18:27.339
And so, I looked at my life

00:18:27.339 --> 00:18:28.507
and said, you know what?

00:18:28.507 --> 00:18:29.475 align:start size:84% position:16%
My life has been
supported and changed

00:18:29.475 --> 00:18:30.709
by the gospel of Jesus Christ.

00:18:30.709 --> 00:18:33.712
And I don't see
a greater message

00:18:33.712 --> 00:18:36.448
or a greater anecdote
or hope for the times

00:18:36.448 --> 00:18:37.916
that we see ourselves in racism.

00:18:37.916 --> 00:18:39.184
And not even that,

00:18:39.184 --> 00:18:40.752
just all the things that
plague the hearts of men

00:18:40.752 --> 00:18:42.488
that I know that the
gospel can change.

00:18:42.488 --> 00:18:44.022
I wanted to stand up
and give that message.

00:18:44.022 --> 00:18:45.491 align:start size:84% position:16%
I didn't wanna go with
anybody's narrative

00:18:45.491 --> 00:18:46.992
or the whole,

00:18:46.992 --> 00:18:48.961
as crazy as the whole Black
Lives Matter movement was.

00:18:48.961 --> 00:18:50.963
I didn't wanna kind
of just fall into it.

00:18:50.963 --> 00:18:52.998
And so I decided to be
the only one to stand

00:18:52.998 --> 00:18:55.501
and to share that message
of loving your neighbor,

00:18:55.501 --> 00:18:57.870 align:start size:84% position:16%
the way that you
were gonna be loved.

00:18:57.870 --> 00:19:00.339 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Did the team know what you
were gonna do on that day

00:19:00.339 --> 00:19:01.540
when you decided to stand

00:19:01.540 --> 00:19:03.442
and everybody else kneeled?

00:19:03.442 --> 00:19:06.044
- So there's a lot of details
in the book that I explained.

00:19:06.044 --> 00:19:09.982
Like, I called somebody that
was in the Magic organization

00:19:09.982 --> 00:19:11.216
the night before.

00:19:11.216 --> 00:19:12.217
'Cause I didn't wanna
catch 'em off guard.

00:19:12.217 --> 00:19:13.485
So I called them

00:19:13.485 --> 00:19:16.722
and we had a whole team
meeting the day before.

00:19:16.722 --> 00:19:17.689
So we had a team meeting

00:19:17.689 --> 00:19:20.125
and the executives of the team,

00:19:20.125 --> 00:19:21.593
came in and said, you know what?

00:19:21.593 --> 00:19:23.695 align:start size:94% position:6%
We support you guys on
whatever you decide to do.

00:19:23.695 --> 00:19:25.964 align:start size:88% position:13%
A team had already
knelt earlier that day.

00:19:25.964 --> 00:19:27.166
And so they were like,

00:19:27.166 --> 00:19:28.100 align:start size:81% position:19%
you were gonna
give you guys time

00:19:28.100 --> 00:19:29.067
to just talk about it as a team,

00:19:29.067 --> 00:19:30.669
so they walked out.

00:19:30.669 --> 00:19:31.603
And the guys were just like,

00:19:31.603 --> 00:19:33.172
yo, we don't have a choice.

00:19:33.172 --> 00:19:34.106
This is what we have to do.

00:19:34.106 --> 00:19:35.340
We have to kneel.

00:19:35.340 --> 00:19:36.808
We can't be only
team that doesn't.

00:19:36.808 --> 00:19:38.477 align:start size:97% position:3%
And then one of my teammates
looking me and they say,

00:19:38.477 --> 00:19:39.645
yo, Jonathan, what
are you gonna do?

00:19:39.645 --> 00:19:41.647 align:start size:88% position:13%
Like, they kind of
knew, I don't know why.

00:19:41.647 --> 00:19:42.981
But he's like, what
are you gonna do?

00:19:42.981 --> 00:19:45.250
I said, fellas, I'm not
gonna wear that t-shirt

00:19:45.250 --> 00:19:46.852
and I'm not gonna kneel
for the national anthem.

00:19:46.852 --> 00:19:48.787
And then I called somebody

00:19:48.787 --> 00:19:50.189 align:start size:88% position:13%
in the Magic
organization that night

00:19:50.189 --> 00:19:51.123
and kind of let 'em know.

00:19:51.123 --> 00:19:52.090
And they just said, okay.

00:19:52.090 --> 00:19:53.325
We'll handle it tomorrow.

00:19:55.227 --> 00:19:56.461
- In retrospect,

00:19:56.461 --> 00:19:57.963
I mean, were you thinking,

00:19:57.963 --> 00:20:00.432
man, like this could cause all
kinds of problems, you know?

00:20:00.432 --> 00:20:02.267
I mean, look, what's going on
with Enes Kanter right now,

00:20:02.267 --> 00:20:03.602 align:start size:84% position:16%
the guys in the
prime of his career,

00:20:03.602 --> 00:20:04.836
he can't get a contract.

00:20:04.836 --> 00:20:07.039
I mean, that it just
creates headaches.

00:20:07.039 --> 00:20:09.408
That even if you have all the
skills and everything else,

00:20:09.408 --> 00:20:10.676
the teams are just like,

00:20:10.676 --> 00:20:11.877
I don't wanna deal
with the headache.

00:20:11.877 --> 00:20:13.278
Everyone else is going along.

00:20:13.278 --> 00:20:15.614
And that's the type of
people we want with us.

00:20:16.682 --> 00:20:19.618
- Look the night before I stood,

00:20:19.618 --> 00:20:21.019 align:start size:81% position:19%
I was on the phone
with my pastor

00:20:21.019 --> 00:20:21.853
and I was letting him know.

00:20:21.853 --> 00:20:23.355
I was like, yo,

00:20:23.355 --> 00:20:25.257 align:start size:97% position:3%
I don't think you understand
how big this is gonna be.

00:20:25.257 --> 00:20:26.825
Like, you know, people
are getting canceled.

00:20:26.825 --> 00:20:29.027
I didn't sign my contract yet.

00:20:29.027 --> 00:20:30.295
I didn't sign my
contract extension.

00:20:30.295 --> 00:20:31.530
So they would,

00:20:31.530 --> 00:20:32.831
and the possibility of
me getting canceled,

00:20:32.831 --> 00:20:33.899
then I wouldn't
have the contract

00:20:33.899 --> 00:20:35.500
that I have right now.

00:20:35.500 --> 00:20:38.203 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
But yeah, I knew the
backlash that was gonna come.

00:20:38.203 --> 00:20:40.672 line:0%
I knew, you know the
Coon and the uncle Tom.

00:20:40.672 --> 00:20:43.075 align:start size:97% position:3%
I know the people who
would automatically take it

00:20:43.075 --> 00:20:45.010 align:start size:94% position:6%
and make it about the flag
in the national anthem,

00:20:45.010 --> 00:20:46.211
and all that stuff.

00:20:46.211 --> 00:20:47.045 align:start size:84% position:16%
I knew all that
stuff was gonna come.

00:20:47.045 --> 00:20:48.347
But at the same time,

00:20:48.347 --> 00:20:49.715
the one thing that my
pastor said to me is,

00:20:49.715 --> 00:20:50.916
you cannot stand for God

00:20:50.916 --> 00:20:52.217
and God cannot stand for you.

00:20:52.217 --> 00:20:53.685
And so, I knew what
I was standing for.

00:20:53.685 --> 00:20:54.853
I wasn't standing
for a movement.

00:20:54.853 --> 00:20:56.154
I wasn't standing for a side.

00:20:56.154 --> 00:20:57.689
I was standing to
offer that message

00:20:57.689 --> 00:20:59.057 align:start size:84% position:16%
that we all fall
show to God's glory,

00:20:59.057 --> 00:21:00.158
every single one of us.

00:21:00.158 --> 00:21:03.295
And with anyone to throw stones

00:21:03.295 --> 00:21:05.230
or throwing stones
from a glass house.

00:21:05.230 --> 00:21:06.598
And so, while I try my best,

00:21:06.598 --> 00:21:08.467
those just kind of come
from a humble position

00:21:08.467 --> 00:21:10.135 align:start size:84% position:16%
and say, man, if we
could love each other,

00:21:10.135 --> 00:21:11.169
the way that God loves us,

00:21:11.169 --> 00:21:12.271
which is in spite of our sin,

00:21:12.271 --> 00:21:13.505
in spite of our faults,

00:21:13.505 --> 00:21:15.307 align:start size:84% position:16%
then we could really
change the world.

00:21:15.307 --> 00:21:17.342
- What about some
of your teammates?

00:21:17.342 --> 00:21:19.278 align:start size:81% position:19%
It sounds like
maybe some of them

00:21:19.278 --> 00:21:20.746
kind of wanted to do the same,

00:21:20.746 --> 00:21:21.747
but felt the pressure

00:21:21.747 --> 00:21:23.181
and just couldn't bear it?

00:21:24.383 --> 00:21:26.685
- Well at the time,
I didn't know that.

00:21:26.685 --> 00:21:28.287
And I wouldn't even say
my teammates per se,

00:21:28.287 --> 00:21:31.023 align:start size:88% position:13%
but I had conversations
with other guys

00:21:31.023 --> 00:21:32.891
around the league and
even in other sports.

00:21:32.891 --> 00:21:34.359
So after I had left the bubble,

00:21:34.359 --> 00:21:35.560
I hurt myself the next game.

00:21:35.560 --> 00:21:36.962
I tore my ACL the next game.

00:21:38.330 --> 00:21:39.965 align:start size:97% position:3%
And I got a call from a
soccer player here in Orlando.

00:21:39.965 --> 00:21:42.467
And he was like, hey,
I saw what you did.

00:21:42.467 --> 00:21:43.568
I wanna do the same thing,

00:21:43.568 --> 00:21:44.670
but I'm terrified.

00:21:44.670 --> 00:21:45.871
And this is a white guy.

00:21:45.871 --> 00:21:47.439
So he's extra terrified.

00:21:47.439 --> 00:21:49.374
(Both chuckles)

00:21:49.374 --> 00:21:50.609
And so, you know,

00:21:50.609 --> 00:21:51.910 align:start size:81% position:19%
I was able to talk
him through it

00:21:51.910 --> 00:21:53.478
and encourage him to stand up

00:21:53.478 --> 00:21:55.280
for what he believes in.

00:21:55.280 --> 00:21:57.516
But you know, it was a
very emotional moment.

00:21:57.516 --> 00:21:59.985 align:start size:84% position:16%
And so I was expecting
guys on my team

00:21:59.985 --> 00:22:01.219
to disagree with me.

00:22:01.219 --> 00:22:02.688 align:start size:84% position:16%
I was even expecting
it to get heated.

00:22:02.688 --> 00:22:04.423 align:start size:84% position:16%
And so, you know,
details in the book,

00:22:04.423 --> 00:22:08.026 align:start size:97% position:3%
there's a team meeting that
happens the day after I stood.

00:22:08.026 --> 00:22:12.064 align:start size:97% position:3%
And it's a heated conversation
between me and the guys.

00:22:12.064 --> 00:22:13.298
But it pretty much ends with,

00:22:13.298 --> 00:22:15.434
look, you guys know for
what you believed in.

00:22:15.434 --> 00:22:16.868 align:start size:84% position:16%
And I stood for
what I believed in.

00:22:16.868 --> 00:22:18.270 align:start size:84% position:16%
It wasn't a protest
for you guys,

00:22:18.270 --> 00:22:19.504
I protest,

00:22:19.504 --> 00:22:20.806
it was just because
I see the same things

00:22:20.806 --> 00:22:22.274
that you guys see,

00:22:22.274 --> 00:22:24.810
but I don't believe that the
Black Lives Matter organization

00:22:24.810 --> 00:22:25.977 align:start size:84% position:16%
or kneeling for
the national anthem

00:22:25.977 --> 00:22:27.746 align:start size:84% position:16%
and wearing a t-shirt
is the answer.

00:22:30.215 --> 00:22:31.717
- What's your take on just sort

00:22:31.717 --> 00:22:34.486 align:start size:94% position:6%
of how generally sports
has become so politicized?

00:22:34.486 --> 00:22:36.254
I mentioned to you when
I saw you in Orlando,

00:22:36.254 --> 00:22:39.291
I grew up the biggest NBA
fan you can ever imagine.

00:22:39.291 --> 00:22:40.792
I mean, basketball,

00:22:40.792 --> 00:22:42.928
I love basketball as much
as you love basketball,

00:22:42.928 --> 00:22:44.463 align:start size:81% position:19%
but I don't really
watch anymore.

00:22:44.463 --> 00:22:47.432
I just don't watch because
it became so politicized.

00:22:47.432 --> 00:22:49.267
Every time I turn
on an NBA game,

00:22:49.267 --> 00:22:51.503 align:start size:94% position:6%
all they're doing is
talking about basketball,

00:22:51.503 --> 00:22:52.704
talking about,

00:22:52.704 --> 00:22:53.672 align:start size:88% position:13%
I wish they were talking
about basketball.

00:22:53.672 --> 00:22:55.574
They're talking about politics

00:22:55.574 --> 00:22:57.676
or they got the BLM logo out,

00:22:57.676 --> 00:23:00.011 align:start size:84% position:16%
or they're analyzing
some race event.

00:23:00.011 --> 00:23:00.946
And I'm just like,

00:23:00.946 --> 00:23:02.948
man, I can't take it anymore.

00:23:02.948 --> 00:23:05.117 align:start size:88% position:13%
Are the players
talking about that too?

00:23:05.117 --> 00:23:06.618 align:start size:84% position:16%
Is there some level
of frustration

00:23:06.618 --> 00:23:09.488
that you guys aren't just
focused on basketball?

00:23:10.856 --> 00:23:14.025 align:start size:97% position:3%
- No, I haven't had that
conversation with any players.

00:23:14.025 --> 00:23:16.628 align:start size:84% position:16%
And I know that
it's something that,

00:23:16.628 --> 00:23:18.797
a large part of
America has felt.

00:23:19.965 --> 00:23:21.299
And I think it's
just unfortunate.

00:23:21.299 --> 00:23:23.969 align:start size:81% position:19%
I think things
like organizations

00:23:23.969 --> 00:23:25.103
like the NBA or anything

00:23:25.103 --> 00:23:27.472 align:start size:84% position:16%
that's in the
entertainment phrase,

00:23:27.472 --> 00:23:31.143
it only benefits them to
be in the middle ground.

00:23:31.143 --> 00:23:34.546
But I think because of,

00:23:34.546 --> 00:23:36.448
maybe one group or
one side being able

00:23:36.448 --> 00:23:39.084
to frame the argument

00:23:39.084 --> 00:23:41.253
and make it a moraL argument

00:23:41.253 --> 00:23:42.487 align:start size:84% position:16%
on a lot of the things
that are happening,

00:23:42.487 --> 00:23:44.089
take the vaccine, take BLM.

00:23:44.089 --> 00:23:45.223
To where if you disagree,

00:23:45.223 --> 00:23:46.525
you're an evil person.

00:23:46.525 --> 00:23:48.059
And so it's easy
for them to kind

00:23:48.059 --> 00:23:49.828
of take that moral
high ground and say,

00:23:49.828 --> 00:23:51.062
this is the only way,

00:23:51.062 --> 00:23:52.764
this is the right way
to handle something.

00:23:52.764 --> 00:23:54.266
But again,

00:23:54.266 --> 00:23:55.767
I think it would be in the
best interest of the NBA

00:23:55.767 --> 00:23:57.335
or any organization to just say,

00:23:58.336 --> 00:23:59.838
we should be in the middle

00:23:59.838 --> 00:24:01.606 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we should allow people
to watch us and enjoy.

00:24:01.606 --> 00:24:04.042
And if an individual player
wants to use their platform

00:24:04.042 --> 00:24:05.544
to speak on something,

00:24:05.544 --> 00:24:07.212
I think that they should have
the absolute right to like,

00:24:07.212 --> 00:24:08.380
I'm doing right now.

00:24:08.380 --> 00:24:10.315 align:start size:88% position:13%
So if anybody in league
wants to stand up

00:24:10.315 --> 00:24:11.450
and say that that was wrong

00:24:11.450 --> 00:24:12.484 align:start size:84% position:16%
or use their
individual platform,

00:24:12.484 --> 00:24:13.718
that's great.

00:24:13.718 --> 00:24:15.787
But I think the NBA
should try their best

00:24:15.787 --> 00:24:17.889
to kind of be in the middle.

00:24:17.889 --> 00:24:18.723
- I agree.

00:24:18.723 --> 00:24:19.925
So, all right.

00:24:19.925 --> 00:24:21.226 align:start size:84% position:16%
So you stand for
the national anthem,

00:24:21.226 --> 00:24:23.094 align:start size:81% position:19%
then you give this
incredible talk

00:24:23.094 --> 00:24:26.665 align:start size:88% position:13%
at the post game on
media day about the vax.

00:24:26.665 --> 00:24:28.967 align:start size:84% position:16%
You get some strange
media reaction.

00:24:28.967 --> 00:24:31.503 align:start size:94% position:6%
Were you kind of surprised
where you were welcomed

00:24:31.503 --> 00:24:34.506
and where you were kind
of shunned after that?

00:24:34.506 --> 00:24:35.740
(Jonathan chuckles)

00:24:35.740 --> 00:24:38.009
- No, I wouldn't say
that I was surprised.

00:24:38.009 --> 00:24:40.312
I definitely, because you know,

00:24:40.312 --> 00:24:42.380
it was during the
national anthem,

00:24:42.380 --> 00:24:44.316
so there's a side of the Al

00:24:44.316 --> 00:24:45.784
that is gonna embrace that.

00:24:45.784 --> 00:24:48.286 align:start size:94% position:6%
And even, the overwhelming
support of Christians

00:24:48.286 --> 00:24:50.789
and everybody that agree
with me on that front.

00:24:50.789 --> 00:24:52.691
So I wasn't surprised at all

00:24:52.691 --> 00:24:53.925
about the calls that I got

00:24:53.925 --> 00:24:55.994
and the different
media personalities

00:24:55.994 --> 00:24:57.295
that wanted to talk
to me afterwards.

00:24:57.295 --> 00:24:59.264
I would say the only thing

00:24:59.264 --> 00:25:01.199 align:start size:84% position:16%
that I maybe was
surprised of was that,

00:25:01.199 --> 00:25:03.235
maybe nobody on the
other side wanted

00:25:03.235 --> 00:25:04.636
to even have a conversation.

00:25:06.271 --> 00:25:08.773
And I think just in the way

00:25:08.773 --> 00:25:10.475 align:start size:84% position:16%
that I kind of
phrased my argument

00:25:10.475 --> 00:25:11.676
or the way I went about it,

00:25:11.676 --> 00:25:12.477 align:start size:84% position:16%
I would've made
more people to say,

00:25:12.477 --> 00:25:13.411
you know what?

00:25:13.411 --> 00:25:14.813
Well, let's just talk about it.

00:25:14.813 --> 00:25:16.248 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, I wasn't
somebody that was saying.

00:25:16.248 --> 00:25:17.449 align:start size:97% position:3%
You know, you guys are
wrong and this is terrible.

00:25:17.449 --> 00:25:18.917 align:start size:84% position:16%
And I didn't come
from that standpoint.

00:25:18.917 --> 00:25:20.719
And so, I would've
definitely been open

00:25:20.719 --> 00:25:22.587 align:start size:97% position:3%
to having more conversations
with the other side.

00:25:22.587 --> 00:25:23.522
But, you know,

00:25:23.522 --> 00:25:24.723
I went where I was welcome

00:25:24.723 --> 00:25:26.258
and I just tried
my best to continue

00:25:26.258 --> 00:25:29.461
to push that Christ first
message and go from there.

00:25:29.461 --> 00:25:31.363
- So let's talk about
the faith part of this.

00:25:31.363 --> 00:25:32.564
'Cause obviously,

00:25:32.564 --> 00:25:33.832
you've mentioned your
faith a few times,

00:25:33.832 --> 00:25:36.735
it's clearly a key
part of your life.

00:25:36.735 --> 00:25:38.236
Were you always a believer?

00:25:38.236 --> 00:25:41.673
Did your family come from a
deep religious background?

00:25:41.673 --> 00:25:44.576
- So I wasn't always a believer,

00:25:44.576 --> 00:25:46.177 align:start size:88% position:13%
but we grew up in church
when we were young

00:25:46.177 --> 00:25:48.113
like all the time.

00:25:48.113 --> 00:25:49.648
We were always in church.

00:25:49.648 --> 00:25:52.817
But then I moved from Bronx,
New York to Naples, Florida,

00:25:52.817 --> 00:25:54.052
and my parents split up.

00:25:54.052 --> 00:25:56.454
And my dad was like my hero,

00:25:56.454 --> 00:25:58.189
but he was really like
the spiritual foundation

00:25:58.189 --> 00:25:59.524
of our family.

00:25:59.524 --> 00:26:02.661 align:start position:0%
And so I went from a
predominantly black neighborhood

00:26:02.661 --> 00:26:04.162
to a predominantly
white neighborhood.

00:26:04.162 --> 00:26:06.331 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I really, really
struggled with fitting in.

00:26:06.331 --> 00:26:09.034
And so I tell in the book
a couple of early instances

00:26:09.034 --> 00:26:10.569
about just how terrible I was

00:26:10.569 --> 00:26:12.470 align:start size:84% position:16%
at getting the other
kids to like me.

00:26:12.470 --> 00:26:13.405
And early on,

00:26:13.405 --> 00:26:15.140
I developed a nickname Ethiopia,

00:26:15.140 --> 00:26:18.310
because I was so skinny and
then obviously, dark skinned.

00:26:18.310 --> 00:26:20.245
And so, it was the first time

00:26:20.245 --> 00:26:21.680 align:start size:84% position:16%
that I became really
self-conscious.

00:26:21.680 --> 00:26:23.648
Like in the New York,
everybody was the same.

00:26:23.648 --> 00:26:24.583
It was fun.

00:26:24.583 --> 00:26:25.350
But once I got to Naples,

00:26:25.350 --> 00:26:26.551
I was like,

00:26:26.551 --> 00:26:28.286
I always tried so hard to fit in

00:26:28.286 --> 00:26:31.489
and to kind of work for
the love of my peers

00:26:31.489 --> 00:26:33.191
that I started to
develop anxiety,

00:26:33.191 --> 00:26:34.526
I started to develop fear,

00:26:34.526 --> 00:26:36.227
and then I found basketball.

00:26:36.227 --> 00:26:38.229
And I was able to kind of put
everything into basketball.

00:26:38.229 --> 00:26:39.531
And that brought me to people,

00:26:39.531 --> 00:26:41.032 align:start size:84% position:16%
the girls that wanted
to be around me,

00:26:41.032 --> 00:26:42.300 align:start size:84% position:16%
the guys that wanted
to be around me.

00:26:42.300 --> 00:26:43.735
I started to make those
friends and those peers,

00:26:43.735 --> 00:26:45.837 align:start position:0%
but I still struggle with
those things in the background.

00:26:45.837 --> 00:26:47.439
And so, I get to Florida state,

00:26:47.439 --> 00:26:48.840
I'm the number one player
in the state of Florida.

00:26:48.840 --> 00:26:51.076
Everybody's expecting me
to be this great player

00:26:51.076 --> 00:26:52.444
that takes 'em to
the championship,

00:26:52.444 --> 00:26:53.712
but I'm still struggling

00:26:53.712 --> 00:26:55.146
with these things
behind the scenes.

00:26:55.146 --> 00:26:57.415 align:start size:97% position:3%
And so I have anxiety
attacks while I'm on campus.

00:26:57.415 --> 00:26:59.584
And I passed out in class and
all these different things.

00:26:59.584 --> 00:27:00.518
And everybody's like,

00:27:00.518 --> 00:27:01.753
what is going on with you?

00:27:03.655 --> 00:27:04.823
But for me,

00:27:04.823 --> 00:27:06.591 align:start size:88% position:13%
and it really is a
wild story in the book.

00:27:06.591 --> 00:27:07.792
I get to the NBA.

00:27:07.792 --> 00:27:08.660
I'm living my life.

00:27:08.660 --> 00:27:09.828
I'm doing my thing.

00:27:09.828 --> 00:27:11.763 align:start size:84% position:16%
And then I get
injured and I guilt.

00:27:11.763 --> 00:27:14.232
I'm at my apartment and
I get on the elevator,

00:27:14.232 --> 00:27:15.467
and that guy stops me.

00:27:15.467 --> 00:27:17.535
And he says, I can tell
you how to be great.

00:27:17.535 --> 00:27:18.737
And I said, tell
me how to be great.

00:27:18.737 --> 00:27:19.571
I'm Jonathan, Isaac,

00:27:19.571 --> 00:27:20.739
what do you mean?

00:27:20.739 --> 00:27:22.173
He's like, you gotta know Jesus.

00:27:22.173 --> 00:27:23.908
And I'm like, Jesus, man.

00:27:23.908 --> 00:27:25.410 align:start size:88% position:13%
Like I grew up Christian
and all this stuff.

00:27:25.410 --> 00:27:26.645
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:27:26.645 --> 00:27:27.912
But from that point on,

00:27:27.912 --> 00:27:30.949
like my life really does
get flipped upside down.

00:27:30.949 --> 00:27:33.885
And it really is a story

00:27:33.885 --> 00:27:35.420 align:start size:88% position:13%
of just like God
revealing himself to me

00:27:35.420 --> 00:27:37.155 align:start size:84% position:16%
and like these
crazy coincidences.

00:27:37.155 --> 00:27:38.356
And ultimately,

00:27:38.356 --> 00:27:39.591
I was able to take a
step back and say like,

00:27:39.591 --> 00:27:40.925
God loves me for me.

00:27:40.925 --> 00:27:44.629
He loves me in spite of
my right and my wrong,

00:27:44.629 --> 00:27:46.131
and I don't have to
work for his love.

00:27:46.131 --> 00:27:47.632 align:start size:84% position:16%
And that was the
first time developing

00:27:47.632 --> 00:27:48.566
that relationship with Christ,

00:27:48.566 --> 00:27:50.301
where I was able to breathe

00:27:50.301 --> 00:27:52.003
and kind of just let
my shoulders sink.

00:27:52.003 --> 00:27:54.072
Like I don't have to
work for his love.

00:27:54.072 --> 00:27:55.907
And I've kind of just
gone down that path

00:27:55.907 --> 00:27:57.242 align:start size:84% position:16%
of developing a
relationship with him.

00:27:57.242 --> 00:27:58.743
And here in Orlando,

00:27:58.743 --> 00:28:00.178
my home church, J.U.M.P.
Ministries Global Church.

00:28:00.178 --> 00:28:02.614
And the story really
does bring to life,

00:28:02.614 --> 00:28:04.449 align:start size:88% position:13%
all those details and
those intricate details.

00:28:04.449 --> 00:28:05.617
I don't wanna give too much away

00:28:05.617 --> 00:28:07.152 align:start size:84% position:16%
because I want people
to go grab them.

00:28:07.152 --> 00:28:08.853
- Oh, we're gonna link to
the book right down below,

00:28:08.853 --> 00:28:10.355
don't worry about that.

00:28:10.355 --> 00:28:12.791
How has your faith been
challenged by the injury?

00:28:12.791 --> 00:28:14.659
Because it's sort
of the nightmare

00:28:14.659 --> 00:28:16.561
of a professional athlete.

00:28:16.561 --> 00:28:17.996
You blow out the knee,

00:28:17.996 --> 00:28:19.564 align:start size:94% position:6%
you blow out the Achilles,
etcetera, etcetera.

00:28:19.564 --> 00:28:21.199
I mean, you're going
through that right now.

00:28:21.199 --> 00:28:23.034
It's been two full seasons.

00:28:23.034 --> 00:28:24.102
- Yeah.

00:28:24.102 --> 00:28:25.503
It's been tough

00:28:25.503 --> 00:28:26.971
and it was really
tough early on.

00:28:26.971 --> 00:28:28.940
But I'm so grateful that I have,

00:28:28.940 --> 00:28:30.842 align:start size:97% position:3%
I just feel like I have
the right people around me.

00:28:30.842 --> 00:28:32.644 align:start size:81% position:19%
Like my pastor,
Dr. Duran Hepburn,

00:28:32.644 --> 00:28:34.612
he's like the angel of the book.

00:28:34.612 --> 00:28:36.981
He's a star in the book
and me coming to faith.

00:28:36.981 --> 00:28:38.850
He's actually the one that
stopped me in that elevator

00:28:38.850 --> 00:28:40.552
and said that to me.

00:28:40.552 --> 00:28:41.753
He's big.

00:28:41.753 --> 00:28:43.154 align:start size:84% position:16%
I mean, my wife is
big, my church family.

00:28:43.154 --> 00:28:44.989
But it was definitely tough.

00:28:44.989 --> 00:28:46.157
Like, you know, asking God,

00:28:46.157 --> 00:28:48.059 align:start size:84% position:16%
like why did you
allow that to happen?

00:28:48.059 --> 00:28:49.394
Like, what's the cause?

00:28:49.394 --> 00:28:51.162
But now that I'm able to
kind of take a step back

00:28:51.162 --> 00:28:53.465
and see that this book is
tangible and it's alive,

00:28:53.465 --> 00:28:54.733
and people are reading it,

00:28:54.733 --> 00:28:56.768
and saying how inspired
and encouraged they are.

00:28:56.768 --> 00:28:57.702
There wouldn't be a book,

00:28:57.702 --> 00:28:58.937
if I didn't get injured.

00:28:58.937 --> 00:29:00.171 align:start size:81% position:19%
I wouldn't have
had time to do it.

00:29:00.171 --> 00:29:01.873 align:start size:88% position:13%
There wouldn't have been
really no inspiration

00:29:01.873 --> 00:29:03.441
to do it outside of just,

00:29:03.441 --> 00:29:05.276 align:start size:97% position:3%
wanting to write a story
about standing in the bubble.

00:29:05.276 --> 00:29:07.112
But the book is so
much more than that.

00:29:07.112 --> 00:29:08.913
The book is really a
journey about my life

00:29:08.913 --> 00:29:10.982
and overcoming fear and anxiety,

00:29:10.982 --> 00:29:13.952
and how a relationship with
Christ helped me to do that.

00:29:13.952 --> 00:29:15.787
And so, it really is
just pointing people

00:29:15.787 --> 00:29:18.323 align:start size:94% position:6%
to what I believe is truly
gonna change the world,

00:29:18.323 --> 00:29:19.557
which is the love of Christ.

00:29:19.557 --> 00:29:23.661
And so, I feel that it
was necessary for me

00:29:23.661 --> 00:29:25.230
to be able to write this book.

00:29:25.230 --> 00:29:26.364
- How does the faith part play

00:29:26.364 --> 00:29:28.433
into just even being in rehab

00:29:28.433 --> 00:29:29.801
and going through the pain,

00:29:29.801 --> 00:29:30.835
going through the surgery,

00:29:30.835 --> 00:29:31.669
all that stuff.

00:29:31.669 --> 00:29:33.037
I mean, I told you,

00:29:33.037 --> 00:29:34.839
my doc wants me to
have the surgery.

00:29:34.839 --> 00:29:37.142 align:start size:81% position:19%
Obviously, I'm
not an NBA player,

00:29:37.142 --> 00:29:38.777 align:start size:84% position:16%
but I've been
prolonging this thing

00:29:38.777 --> 00:29:39.978
and I don't really wanna do it.

00:29:39.978 --> 00:29:41.346
And I got PRP in my knee

00:29:41.346 --> 00:29:43.248
and it's feeling pretty good.

00:29:43.248 --> 00:29:44.616
But just the process,

00:29:44.616 --> 00:29:46.451
'cause how long are
you just laid out

00:29:46.451 --> 00:29:49.921 align:start size:94% position:6%
when you have the ACL
surgery just fully in bed?

00:29:49.921 --> 00:29:50.755
- It was a while.

00:29:50.755 --> 00:29:52.123
I think for me,

00:29:52.123 --> 00:29:54.192 align:start size:97% position:3%
it was a little more
complicated than just the ACL.

00:29:54.192 --> 00:29:57.796 align:start size:88% position:13%
And so, I was in bed
for at least two months.

00:29:57.796 --> 00:30:01.432
And then non-weight
bearing after that

00:30:01.432 --> 00:30:02.767
for another month or so.

00:30:04.235 --> 00:30:05.069
And so, yeah.

00:30:05.069 --> 00:30:06.337
But I think for me,

00:30:06.337 --> 00:30:08.239
in recovery is just like
the faith thing helps me

00:30:08.239 --> 00:30:09.908 align:start size:97% position:3%
because I know that there's
a purpose behind it.

00:30:09.908 --> 00:30:12.610
And so, what I've learned
through getting injured

00:30:12.610 --> 00:30:14.379 align:start size:88% position:13%
and being able to write
this book is like,

00:30:14.379 --> 00:30:15.847
ultimately what God happens,

00:30:15.847 --> 00:30:17.115
what happens good or bad,

00:30:17.115 --> 00:30:18.750
God does have a purpose for it.

00:30:18.750 --> 00:30:20.552
And there's a verse in
the Bible that says,

00:30:20.552 --> 00:30:22.620 align:start size:84% position:16%
"All things work
together for the good,

00:30:22.620 --> 00:30:23.755
to them that love God

00:30:23.755 --> 00:30:24.823 align:start size:88% position:13%
and are called according
to his purpose."

00:30:24.823 --> 00:30:26.324
So all I have to worry about

00:30:26.324 --> 00:30:29.527 line:0%
is loving God and aiming
to please him with my life.

00:30:29.527 --> 00:30:31.062 line:0%
And he's gonna make sure

00:30:31.062 --> 00:30:32.630 line:0%
that all the good and the
bad work towards my good.

00:30:32.630 --> 00:30:34.833 align:start size:81% position:19%
And so, I see that
with this book.

00:30:34.833 --> 00:30:36.901
I see that the people
leading the reviews

00:30:36.901 --> 00:30:38.336
and it inspiring them.

00:30:38.336 --> 00:30:40.805 align:start size:97% position:3%
And I got a message to
yesterday about a guy saying,

00:30:40.805 --> 00:30:41.973
you know what?

00:30:41.973 --> 00:30:43.408 align:start size:88% position:13%
I'm really gonna
pursue this faith thing

00:30:43.408 --> 00:30:45.176 align:start size:97% position:3%
and figure out what a
relationship with Jesus Christ

00:30:45.176 --> 00:30:46.144
because your book.

00:30:46.144 --> 00:30:47.412
And so, I'm like, man,

00:30:47.412 --> 00:30:48.680 align:start size:81% position:19%
okay, I can see
the purpose in it.

00:30:48.680 --> 00:30:50.415
And so, with going through rehab

00:30:50.415 --> 00:30:52.417 align:start size:88% position:13%
with the day-in,
day-out monotonous work

00:30:52.417 --> 00:30:53.918 align:start size:84% position:16%
that does get
tiring and gruesome.

00:30:53.918 --> 00:30:55.854
I'm like, man, there's a
purpose behind all of this.

00:30:55.854 --> 00:30:58.523
And I just can't wait to
get back onto the court.

00:30:58.523 --> 00:31:00.792
- How do you live a
life that's pretty,

00:31:00.792 --> 00:31:01.626
from what I could tell,

00:31:01.626 --> 00:31:02.560
pretty straight laced.

00:31:02.560 --> 00:31:04.562
And I did meet your girlfriend,

00:31:04.562 --> 00:31:05.797
who's fantastic.

00:31:05.797 --> 00:31:08.466
Like compared to
what we think of,

00:31:08.466 --> 00:31:10.468
say the average NBA
player out there,

00:31:10.468 --> 00:31:11.669
partying all night,

00:31:11.669 --> 00:31:13.171 align:start size:84% position:16%
going to strip clubs,
blah, blah, blah.

00:31:13.171 --> 00:31:15.840 align:start size:94% position:6%
How do you kind of
grapple those two things,

00:31:15.840 --> 00:31:18.209
like figure out
who your crew is,

00:31:18.209 --> 00:31:19.878
and all that kind of thing?

00:31:19.878 --> 00:31:21.412
- Well, I mean, I guess,

00:31:21.412 --> 00:31:23.715
I just try to live my
life authentically.

00:31:23.715 --> 00:31:25.516
Like I've experienced that.

00:31:25.516 --> 00:31:26.718
Like I'm not one to say,

00:31:26.718 --> 00:31:28.186
like I haven't,

00:31:28.186 --> 00:31:29.921
wasn't the one that was going
to the clubs and drinking,

00:31:29.921 --> 00:31:31.189
and do all the stuff I was.

00:31:31.189 --> 00:31:33.091
And I got to experience
and I got to figure out

00:31:33.091 --> 00:31:34.292
that it's empty, man.

00:31:34.292 --> 00:31:37.095
It's not something
that can sustain you.

00:31:37.095 --> 00:31:39.030 align:start size:97% position:3%
It's something that's
pleasurable for the moment.

00:31:39.030 --> 00:31:40.665 align:start size:88% position:13%
And then you wake up and
your head is hurting,

00:31:40.665 --> 00:31:42.667 align:start size:81% position:19%
and you gotta deal
with everything

00:31:42.667 --> 00:31:44.135
that happened the night before.

00:31:44.135 --> 00:31:45.103
And so, you know,

00:31:45.103 --> 00:31:46.704
that there's a verse that says,

00:31:46.704 --> 00:31:48.673
"Jesus came that
we may have life

00:31:48.673 --> 00:31:50.241
and have life more abundantly."

00:31:50.241 --> 00:31:52.110 align:start size:84% position:16%
And when I was doing
all those things

00:31:52.110 --> 00:31:53.578
and living that early NBA life,

00:31:53.578 --> 00:31:54.879
I really thought
that I was living.

00:31:54.879 --> 00:31:56.047
And I really thought
that I had the life

00:31:56.047 --> 00:31:57.715
that everybody wanted.

00:31:57.715 --> 00:32:00.385
But what I've been
able to experience in
the last four years

00:32:00.385 --> 00:32:01.653 align:start size:94% position:6%
in developing a
relationship with Christ,

00:32:01.653 --> 00:32:03.288
like I wasn't even
close to living.

00:32:03.288 --> 00:32:04.889
And being able to
do what I do now,

00:32:04.889 --> 00:32:07.926
write a book and just see
my life kind of expand.

00:32:07.926 --> 00:32:08.993
And I'm married now,

00:32:08.993 --> 00:32:09.794
all those different things.

00:32:09.794 --> 00:32:10.795
It's like, man, like,

00:32:10.795 --> 00:32:12.096
it really is the truth.

00:32:12.096 --> 00:32:14.999
And so I just try
to live my life.

00:32:14.999 --> 00:32:16.234
But at the same time,

00:32:16.234 --> 00:32:17.035
I have the right
people around me.

00:32:17.035 --> 00:32:18.236
I have accountability

00:32:18.236 --> 00:32:19.604 align:start size:84% position:16%
that helps keep me
strong and structured.

00:32:19.604 --> 00:32:20.805
And I just kind of
keep my head down

00:32:20.805 --> 00:32:22.240
and just keep moving forward.

00:32:23.641 --> 00:32:27.145 align:start size:97% position:3%
- What do you wanna do when
the NBA thing wraps up?

00:32:27.145 --> 00:32:28.279
(Jonathan chuckles)

00:32:28.279 --> 00:32:29.247
- This is everybody-

00:32:29.247 --> 00:32:31.015
- I sense something here.

00:32:31.015 --> 00:32:32.283
- Yeah.

00:32:32.283 --> 00:32:34.686
Listen, everybody
kind of, you know.

00:32:34.686 --> 00:32:35.520
And I won't say everybody,

00:32:35.520 --> 00:32:37.088
but a lot of people say,

00:32:37.088 --> 00:32:38.556 align:start size:84% position:16%
you need to go on
and become a pastor,

00:32:38.556 --> 00:32:39.757
all these different things.

00:32:39.757 --> 00:32:43.094
But I'm always hesitant
to even affirm that,

00:32:43.094 --> 00:32:46.831 align:start size:97% position:3%
just because I see firsthand
how difficult it is

00:32:46.831 --> 00:32:48.232
and how high of a calling it is

00:32:48.232 --> 00:32:50.969
to kind of shepherd
people through life.

00:32:50.969 --> 00:32:53.471
But I mean, I wouldn't say no.

00:32:53.471 --> 00:32:54.739
But I think right now,

00:32:54.739 --> 00:32:56.474 align:start size:81% position:19%
I'm just trying
to figure out more

00:32:56.474 --> 00:32:58.209
and more what God's
plan for my life.

00:32:58.209 --> 00:33:00.445
I'm working on a second book.

00:33:00.445 --> 00:33:02.213 align:start size:84% position:16%
The "Why I Stand"
book is being talked

00:33:02.213 --> 00:33:03.982
about turning into a movie.

00:33:03.982 --> 00:33:05.483
- Wow.

00:33:05.483 --> 00:33:06.718
- And so there's just a lot
going on and I'm excited.

00:33:06.718 --> 00:33:09.287
I just want to continue
to be a beacon of hope

00:33:09.287 --> 00:33:11.556
for people who have
struggle with anxiety

00:33:11.556 --> 00:33:12.824
and depression, and fear,

00:33:12.824 --> 00:33:13.958
and let them know
that there is hope

00:33:13.958 --> 00:33:15.360
in a relationship with Christ,

00:33:15.360 --> 00:33:17.562 align:start size:84% position:16%
people who struggle
with suicide.

00:33:17.562 --> 00:33:18.830
And just continue
to move forward.

00:33:18.830 --> 00:33:22.166
Like I want to help the
world be a better place.

00:33:22.166 --> 00:33:24.635 align:start position:0%
And I think the message of
Jesus Christ is how we do that.

00:33:24.635 --> 00:33:27.038
And that's just where I'm at.

00:33:27.038 --> 00:33:28.272
- By the way, we should mention,

00:33:28.272 --> 00:33:29.640 align:start size:88% position:13%
so the Daily Wire, which
you mentioned before,

00:33:29.640 --> 00:33:31.409 align:start size:88% position:13%
they are the
publishers of the book.

00:33:31.409 --> 00:33:34.512
And is the movie going
through Daily Wire too?

00:33:34.512 --> 00:33:36.147
Are you allowed to say?

00:33:36.147 --> 00:33:37.648
- Yeah, yes.

00:33:37.648 --> 00:33:39.717
So they're gonna be a part of
bringing the movie to life.

00:33:39.717 --> 00:33:40.551
We're just still-

00:33:40.551 --> 00:33:41.786
- Wow, awesome.

00:33:41.786 --> 00:33:43.588
- Bringing it around
to other entities.

00:33:43.588 --> 00:33:44.822
So we're figuring it out.

00:33:44.822 --> 00:33:45.923
But I think it's
gonna be something

00:33:45.923 --> 00:33:47.425 align:start size:88% position:13%
that's really
inspiring, really dope.

00:33:47.425 --> 00:33:49.727 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you know, something
that a family can sit down

00:33:49.727 --> 00:33:52.363
and watch, and be inspired by.

00:33:52.363 --> 00:33:54.298
- I think people got
most of your message.

00:33:54.298 --> 00:33:57.602 align:start size:88% position:13%
But is there any last
message I can offer them

00:33:57.602 --> 00:34:00.438
or that you can offer
them that you want?

00:34:00.438 --> 00:34:03.408
- Right now, "Why I Stand."

00:34:03.408 --> 00:34:04.342
I got the book right here,

00:34:04.342 --> 00:34:05.710
just so you guys can see it.

00:34:05.710 --> 00:34:07.879
But yeah, go to Amazon, grab it.

00:34:07.879 --> 00:34:09.480
Again, the book is so much more

00:34:09.480 --> 00:34:11.716 align:start size:84% position:16%
than just about
standing in the bubble

00:34:12.950 --> 00:34:14.152
and refusing a vaccine.

00:34:14.152 --> 00:34:15.653 align:start size:84% position:16%
It really is a story
about my journey

00:34:15.653 --> 00:34:17.955 align:start size:97% position:3%
and how I got to those
moments in the first place.

00:34:17.955 --> 00:34:21.926
And so, I believe it to be
encouraging and inspiring.

00:34:21.926 --> 00:34:24.495
And even if you're
not a Christian,

00:34:24.495 --> 00:34:27.598
read the book and you
may walk away one.

00:34:27.598 --> 00:34:29.033
But yeah,

00:34:29.033 --> 00:34:30.668 align:start position:0%
so I just wanna encourage
people to go ahead and grab it.

00:34:30.668 --> 00:34:31.903
It's doing great on Amazon.

00:34:31.903 --> 00:34:35.273
We're gonna find out
tomorrow or Thursday,

00:34:35.273 --> 00:34:37.875 align:start size:97% position:3%
if we made the New York Times
best sellers list or not.

00:34:37.875 --> 00:34:39.110
So we're praying that we did,

00:34:39.110 --> 00:34:40.945
but it's just an exciting time.

00:34:40.945 --> 00:34:42.713 align:start size:94% position:6%
And again, just encourage
people to go grab it.

00:34:42.713 --> 00:34:44.315
- I hate to tell you my friend,

00:34:44.315 --> 00:34:47.118
as an old grizzled
veteran of books,

00:34:47.118 --> 00:34:48.519 align:start size:84% position:16%
